SECTION: CONTACT (Earth / The Cave)

Vibe: Ancient, quiet, and tactile. A secret chamber discovered at the end
of a long journey.
Goal: Transform a standard, boring "Contact Me" list into a memorable moment
of discovery using lighting and masking mechanics.

GLOBAL CONTAINER & ARCHITECTURE

Background: #000000 (Pure Pitch Black).

Layout: Center-aligned content container, min-height: 100vh.

Z-Index Layering (Crucial for the effect):

Z-Index 1 (Bottom): The actual content (Text, Links, Artifact).

Z-Index 2 (Middle): A subtle, dark rock texture image (mix-blend-mode: multiply).

Z-Index 3 (Top): The "Darkness" overlay mask.

LAYOUT ELEMENTS & TYPOGRAPHY (The Hidden Content)

[ A. Section Header ]

Text: CARVED IN STONE

Typography: Syne, 64px (or text-5xl to text-7xl fluid), Weight 800.

Color: #FCD34D (Warm Amber), with an intrinsic subtle drop shadow:
drop-shadow(0 0 15px rgba(252, 211, 77, 0.4)).

Layout: Centered at the top of the content block.

[ B. Contact Links ]

Layout: A 2x2 grid centered on the screen.

Items: Resume, GitHub, LinkedIn, Email.

Typography: Space Grotesk, 24px to 32px.

Default Color: #D6D3D1 (Sandy/Ash Gray).

Hover State: Text color shifts to #FFFFFF, and a small right-facing arrow →
fades in from the left (opacity: 0 to opacity: 1, transform: translateX(5px)).

[ C. The Ancient Artifact ]

Positioning: At the very bottom center of the section.

Visual: The t.tofu logo, but rendered in the "Ancient" style (dark brown/gray
stone texture, heavy shadows, no neon).

MICRO-INTERACTION 1: THE FLASHLIGHT CURSOR

When the user arrives, the screen is almost entirely black. They must use their
mouse to read the wall.

The Darkness Overlay (Z-Index 3):

A div covering the entire viewport: position: absolute; inset: 0; background: #000;

The Mask Logic:

The Darkness overlay has a CSS mask applied:
-webkit-mask-image: radial-gradient(circle 250px at var(--mouse-x, 50%) var(--mouse-y, 50%), transparent 0%, black 100%);

As the mouse moves, the var(--mouse-x) and var(--mouse-y) are updated
via a requestAnimationFrame loop.

Visual Result: A 250px "hole" is cut into the pitch-black overlay, revealing
the glowing amber text and rock texture strictly underneath the cursor.

MICRO-INTERACTION 2: IGNITING THE TORCH

A secret mechanism that allows the user to turn the lights on permanently.

The Torch Bracket:

Positioning: Fixed to the top-left or middle-left wall of the cave.

Visual (Unlit): A faint, dark geometric outline of a sconce/bracket. It is
barely visible even when the flashlight shines on it.

Affordance: When the flashlight passes over it, a tiny, faint text prompt
fades in: [ Ignite Torch ] (DM Sans, 12px, #D6D3D1, opacity: 0.5).

The Click Event (Ignition):

When the user clicks the torch bracket, it triggers the setLit(true) state.

Animation 1 (The Flame): A bright #F97316 (Orange/Plasma) circle blooms
from the bracket, utilizing animate-pulse and heavy filter: blur().

Animation 2 (Banish the Dark): The Darkness Overlay (Z-Index 3) fades its
opacity from 1 to 0 over 1.5 seconds (transition: opacity 1.5s ease-out).

Animation 3 (Ambient Light): The rock texture layer (Z-Index 2) warms up,
shifting its color tint slightly toward amber to simulate firelight.

Post-Ignition State:

The flashlight cursor is disabled.

The user's mouse reverts to a standard pointer.

The entire cave is now fully visible, bathed in a warm, flickering glow.

All contact links are fully accessible and readable without hunting.

TECHNICAL UX & PERFORMANCE NOTES

Accessibility: Do NOT use display: none on the text when the lights are out,
or screen readers won't find it. The text must always exist in the DOM; it
is only visually obscured by the Z-Index 3 black overlay.

Performance: CSS mask-image is highly performant. Update the CSS custom
properties (--mouse-x) on the container, not on the individual text elements,
to minimize recalculations.